     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). Doses that high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nCan you check what was intended? A few possibilities:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the max for immediate-release, and 1700 mg may be a typo for it.\n- **1700 mg total daily.** That could be given as 850 mg twice daily with meals.\n- **500 mg to 1000 mg twice daily.** This is the typical range.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly and give a reason for the note on the order."
      }
     ],
